{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/631917-coding-initiative-issues-and-choices","id":631917,"title":"Coding initiative: issues and choices","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-18T22:42:45-07:00","id":631917,"title":"Coding initiative: issues and choices","content":"Right! The coding is progressing, and results should be available &quot;soon&quot;, for some value of &quot;soon&quot;. And I've had to make some choices and resolve some ambiguities in the rules.<br /> <br /> Using the vampire rules (the reason: those rules don't assign varying difficulties for defending against different attacks), the main problem is initiative rolls. Every single choice available to the characters doubles the size of their choice set, multiplies the joint choice set by four, and probably multiplies the time taken for the algorithm to converge by sixteen or so.<br /> <br /> But what choices are involved in the initiative roll? Quite simply, the initiative roll is penalised by wound penalties - but a character can choose to spend willpower/rage to ignore wound penalties. More seriously, a character adds their celerity to the roll - but only celerity not used for extra actions that turn. Which means character have to make decisions before anyone rolls for initiative, and celerity users (alone of all the multiple attack people) have to decide their number of extra actions in advance (and maybe simultaneously with others, which is another issue - see later).<br /> <br /> So I decided on this solution: character roll their initiative at the end of the previous turn. All wound penalties, celerity available, etc... depend on choices made in that previous turn, so rolling initiative is clear and simple. Anyone feel strong objections to this idea?<br /> <br /> Since it could arguably advantage celerity users (they can launch a flurry of high initiative attacks, and if it kills their opponent, they don't care about the next, low-initiative turn), characters would get penalised of half their celerity during the initiative roll for the first turn.<br /> <br /> The next issue is what happens when two initiative rolls are equal. Attacks happening simultaneously is fine. Decisions happening simultaneously is much more complicated. Basically, if the character decisions happen one after another, you can set up a decision tree and solve it that way. If they happen simultaneously, you have to use game theory and search for a Nash equilibrium, which is much more complicated.<br /> <br /> So I decided that &quot;equal initiative&quot; meant &quot;each character has a 50/50 chance of making their decisions first&quot;. Any issues with that?<br /> <br /> Cheers for your help!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","user":"Cheesefondue","date":". 08-19-2015, 01:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T23:16:18-07:00","id":632014,"title":"","content":"It'd nerf Spirit of the Fray, if someone took Hummingbird as a totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T02:57:32-07:00","id":632111,"title":"","content":"Spirit of the Fray is kinda the staple of Werewolf combat. Turn One Half Rage. Turn Two Half Rage. Turn three, everything is dead or it's really time to run the hell away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T09:44:34-07:00","id":632406,"title":"","content":"Simlpe SotF nerf:<br /> <br /> Change the constant effect to always getting a 10 on the initiative roll rather than adding 10. The Gnosis still does as noted (which makes Hummingbird a non-problem since burning Gnosis a lot with Hummingbird as a Totem is harsh). So an Ahroun with Dex 4/Wits 4, defaults to a rolled initiative of 18, rather than a range of 19 to 28.<br /> <br /> ------------<br /> <br /> As for ties in the computations:<br /> <br /> There is a sorting algorithm in the books (didn't make it into V20 for whatever reason) for a tied roll, and declarations:<br /> <br /> If tied rolls, use initiative rating. If tied rating, use highest Dex or Wits. If everything is tied, have those characters re-roll just to determine declaration order (which is essentially a 50/50).<br /> <br /> Though in play, as opposed to in computation, simultaneous declarations aren't that hard. Both players tell the ST secretly (whisper in their ear, pass a note, text them, whatever); so neither is declaring without an advantage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T13:06:08-07:00","id":632647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/631917-coding-initiative-issues-and-choices?p=632014#post632014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It'd nerf Spirit of the Fray, if someone took Hummingbird as a totem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fortunately, level 2 gifts aren't available for starting players. But I don't see why this would be a nerf; +10 to initiative almost always makes them go first.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T13:13:09-07:00","id":632682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheesefondue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/631917-coding-initiative-issues-and-choices?p=632647#post632647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fortunately, level 2 gifts aren't available for starting players.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was why I specified someone who took Hummingbird as a totem. It gives you Spirit of the Fray.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T14:39:23-07:00","id":632723,"title":"","content":"if someone takes humminbird as a totem, it's super-easy to keep them in line. That sucker needs one gnosis per day, and while Gnosis isn't the most difficult of point-spending traits to regain... it's certainly not the easiest, either. Especially if your pack is prone to you know, using Gifts and rites. And it's a totem of War, so presumably your pack is going to be out there fighting, more than at the caern meditating. <br /> <br /> That said, that WAS a totem that spurred me to change spirit of the fray in my online game (where Gnosis is rather harder to track, making hummingbird much less punishing...) My Spirit of the Fray lets you add one die to your initiative roll for each Rank you have, and keep the highest. You can spend a Gnosis to bunk your spot up (but not any packmates) by one on the initiative chart. <br /> <br /> Auto-10 is definitely smoother, and I'm debating giving a change now that I see it and go &quot;huh.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T16:58:41-07:00","id":632829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cat Came Back</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/631917-coding-initiative-issues-and-choices?p=632723#post632723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if someone takes humminbird as a totem, it's super-easy to keep them in line.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that we were talking about short-range tactical simulations, not long haul stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T00:02:27-07:00","id":633216,"title":"","content":"Given the intent, I think Hummingbird is a non-issue.<br /> <br /> Not that it can't appear in the simulations. It can. Its just that I don't see why bother. The rule proposed is for Celerity, only. It shouldn't affect Spirit of the Fray.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T13:39:12-07:00","id":633752,"title":"","content":"At long last, clinching is coded and tested ^_^<br /> <br /> And there's at least one indication (one test I ran) that the vampires might not do so badly as I expected when clinch is an option - probably because they now have the Kiss.<br /> <br /> And, for initiative, I've decided on a simple solution: celerity characters get their full celerity for the initiative roll *for the purposes of determining who chooses their actions first*. However, they subtract from this initiative for every extra action they add, so they may end up striking second. It's a little bit biased towards the celerity (and everyone knows that celerity is already the most underpowered discipline in the game), but it's very, very easy to code the way I have things set up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}